## GIS Designer

**Location:** Marion, NC | **Type:** Full-Time

### Job Summary

We are seeking a skilled GIS Designer to join our growing team. The GIS Designer will be responsible for creating and maintaining accurate GIS data, conducting spatial analysis, and supporting the design of fiber optic networks. This role requires proficiency in GIS software and a strong understanding of fiber optic network infrastructure.

### Responsibilities

- Develop and maintain GIS data for fiber optic network projects
- Create spatial analysis reports and maps to support project planning and design
- Collaborate with engineering and construction teams to ensure accurate representation of network designs
- Perform quality control on GIS data to ensure accuracy and completeness
- Support permitting efforts by preparing GIS-based maps and documentation
- Integrate GIS data with CAD tools for construction drawing production

- Stay updated on advancements in GIS technology and fiber optic design practices

### Qualifications

- Bachelor's degree in GIS, Geography, Computer Science, or a related field
- Minimum of 2 years of experience in GIS design, preferably in telecommunications
- Proficiency in Esri ArcGIS (ArcMap/ArcGIS Pro)
- Experience with CAD software (AutoCAD or MicroStation preferred)
- Knowledge of fiber optic network design principles
- Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail

### Benefits

- Competitive compensation
- Paid time off
- Health benefits
- 401k
- Equipment provided

[Apply Now](#)
</tool_response>

