## OSP Designer

**Location:** Marion, NC | **Type:** Full-Time

### Job Summary

We are seeking an experienced OSP Designer to join our team. The OSP Designer will be responsible for designing outside plant fiber optic networks, including route planning, splice plans, and construction drawing production. This role requires a strong understanding of fiber optic design standards and proficiency in industry design tools.

### Responsibilities

- Design outside plant fiber optic networks including route planning, splice plans, and fiber assignment
- Produce construction drawings and permit packages for regulatory review and approval
- Coordinate with permitting agencies, utilities, and municipalities for ROW and permit approvals
- Collaborate with GIS team to ensure design data is accurately represented in GIS
- Review and quality check designs for accuracy and compliance with standards

- Perform site walks and field verification to support design accuracy
- Manage design deliverables and timelines to support construction schedules

### Qualifications

- Minimum of 3 years of experience in OSP fiber optic design
- Proficiency in AutoCAD or MicroStation
- Experience with GIS platforms (ArcGIS preferred)
- Familiarity with permitting processes for NCDOT, utility poles, and municipalities
- Knowledge of BEAD or government-funded program requirements is a plus
- Strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously

### Benefits

- Competitive compensation
- Paid time off
- Health benefits
- 401k
- Equipment provided

[Apply Now](#)
